From: =?utf-8?b?Ik1hcmNvIFRyZXZpc2FuIChUcmV2acOxbyki?= <mail@3v1n0.net>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 02:21:15 +0200
Subject: userVerifier: Do not allow any other service to take control of the
 UI

Authentication services share the same user verifier. Once a mechanism is
selected, only its service should be able to update the prompt or otherwise
take control of the UI, except for services exposing background mechanisms.

Track the selected service separately from the per-service selected
mechanism. This allows filtering service-scoped signals, including resets,
when they are emitted by a service that is not controlling verification.

The selected service may stop exposing a mechanism after available roles are
updated. In that case, do not leave the UI without a selected mechanism:
fall back to the first auto-selectable mechanism instead.

This prevents background or unrelated services from taking over the prompt
while keeping selection valid when the set of available mechanisms changes.
